                           (default info; results always go to stdout)
  --help                   Show help
  --version                Show version

A checkpoint stores solver state -- velocity, pressure, the corrected face
mass flux, the completed iteration count and the residual history -- so a
resumed run continues the same solve instead of starting a new one.
Resuming needs the same mesh and the same case configuration; only
solver.json max_iterations may differ, so a run can be given more
iterations and finished.
